		{
			"identifier": "GroundItem",
			"uid": 5943,
			"tags": [],
			"exportToToc": false,
			"allowOutOfBounds": true,
			"doc": "A held item (gauntlet or weapon) resting on the ground, pick-up-able with Attack while empty-handed. `held_item` is a brain held-item registry id (e.g. meteor, bomb, blink, grapple, gun_sword) resolved at spawn; the box size sets the pickup half-extent. Replaces the debug spawn_debug_ground_items_once table with authored placement. `regrow_seconds`, when set, makes the placement a source: once nothing of its kind lies there, a fresh one appears after that many seconds (a palm's coconut). `regrow_limit`, when set, caps how many of the items it grew may lie loose in its room at once (a tree's apples fall away from it, so without one it would drop apples without end). `hang_seconds`, when set, hangs the item where it is placed that long before it drops (an apple ripening on its tree), the placed item and each one it grows.",
			"width": 28,
			"height": 28,
			"resizableX": true,
